<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 320 bln lire of Italy CCTs.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 320 bln lire of Italy CCTs.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 320 billion lire of seven-year variable-rate certificates (CCTs) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 300 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 9.067 trillion lire at the open auction for the March 1, 2004 paper, against three trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 99.40 from 99.00 at the previous CCT sale on March 27.</p>
</text>
